{"name":"Eye Popping Cherry","hex":"#bb0077","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).","The visual sense."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carefully or appraisingly observe (someone or something).","To consider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye"},{"term":"popping","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very lively."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or sound of something that pops.","A style of funk dance involving rapid contractions and relaxations of the muscles to switch between poses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/popping"},{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Popping Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"\"Popping Cherry\" is the third episode of the first season of the American crime drama television series Dexter. The episode was written by co-executive producer Daniel Cerone, and directed by co-executive producer Michael Cuesta. It originally aired on Showtime on October 15, 2006."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png/330px-James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popping_Cherry","wikidata":"Q12089742"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"},{"title":"Popping","blocks":[{"text":"Popping is a street dance adapted out of the earlier boogaloo cultural movement in Oakland, California. As boogaloo spread, it would be referred to as \"robottin'\" in Richmond, California; Strutting movements in San Francisco and San Jose; and the Strikin' dances of the Oak Park community in Sacramento, and \"Pop-Locking\" of Los Angeles which were popular through the mid-1960s to the late 1970s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Popping.jpg/330px-Popping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popping","wikidata":"Q937440"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png/330px-James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png/330px-James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/500px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/1280px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm